# Rate Limiting Environment Variables

Add these to your `.env` file:

```env
# Enable or disable rate limiting globally
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=true

# Cache store to use for rate limit data
# Options: array, database, file, memcached, redis, dynamodb, octane
RATE_LIMIT_CACHE_STORE=cache

# IPs that should bypass rate limiting (comma-separated)
# Useful for internal monitoring, load balancers, etc.
RATE_LIMIT_BYPASS_IPS=127.0.0.1

# Cache configuration (used if CACHE_STORE=database)
CACHE_STORE=database
DB_CACHE_CONNECTION=
DB_CACHE_TABLE=cache
```

## Cache Store Options

### Database (Recommended for Development)
```env
RATE_LIMIT_CACHE_STORE=cache
CACHE_STORE=database
```

### Redis (Recommended for Production)
```env
RATE_LIMIT_CACHE_STORE=redis
CACHE_STORE=redis
REDIS_HOST=127.0.0.1
REDIS_PASSWORD=null
REDIS_PORT=6379
```

### Memcached (Alternative for Production)
```env
RATE_LIMIT_CACHE_STORE=memcached
CACHE_STORE=memcached
MEMCACHED_HOST=127.0.0.1
MEMCACHED_PORT=11211
```

### File (Not Recommended)
```env
RATE_LIMIT_CACHE_STORE=file
CACHE_STORE=file
```
